WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.480
Hey Wisecrack, Jared here.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.290
Today, we’ve got a favorite among the Wisecrack
staff.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.559
The tale of humans picked for experimental
augmentations, to find out what happens when

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.789
people stop being polite and start getting
real.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:20.910
At first look, the Deus Ex franchise is a
kind of wet dream for InfoWars enthusiasts:

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.759
murderous plots by the Illuminati are carried
out by world governments, while the player

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:28.920
traverses FEMA camps and discovers the truth
behind fake news.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.649
But unlike certain performance artists — “AHHHH!”

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:37.730
— Deus Ex’s forays into conspiracy serve
as more than just a means to sell dietary

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:38.730
supplements.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.220
The game reveals how paranoia informs more
of society’s decisions that we’d like

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.550
to admit, and serves as a cautionary tale
for the dangers of technology-to-come.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.960
But there are no gay frogs.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:49.960
Sorry, internet.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.960
"I don't like them putting chemicals in the
water that turn the friggin’ frogs gay!"

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.390
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on Deus
Ex.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.940
This video was made in collaboration with
our buddy, Joseph, over at Real Life Lore.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.420
You can learn more about his channel and check
out his related video and the end of this

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.420
one.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.659
And if you’re here visiting from Real Life
Lore, welcome and be sure to subscribe.

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:11.240
And spoilers ahead, for all the games.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.799
The Deus Ex series asks two basic questions:
1) What would it mean for society if we could

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:19.460
all become cyborgs with Jax-arms?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:24.399
And 2) What does the premise that every conspiracy
theory is true mean for the real world?

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:28.399
And before we get into the ethics of skull-guns
and neural enhancement, we have to put on

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:30.409
our tinfoil hats.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:34.060
There is no shortage of conspiracy theories
in the Deus Ex series.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.859
In the original game, a splinter organization
of the Illuminati called Majestic-12 produces

00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:43.409
a nanite virus called “The Grey Death”
as a means to consolidate their power.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:44.920
"Why contain it?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.719
Let it spill over to the schools, and churches,
let the bodies pile up in the streets.

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:52.350
In the end, they'll beg us to save them.”

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:57.080
As producers of the only cure for the disease
as well, they can easily manipulate others,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.549
while capitalizing off of the disorder wrought
by it.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:02.249
"The Grey Death is a manmade disease.

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:06.039
Everyone up to the president is at UNATCO's
mercy as long as UNATCO controls the supply

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:07.039
of ambrosia."

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:11.300
In the sequel, Invisible War, the Illuminati
controls two of the most influential groups

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.230
in the world: The World Trade Organization,
and The Order, a religious organization opposed

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.330
to the WTO.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:21.860
By managing the conflict between these two
factions, the Illuminati is better able to

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.360
control the world.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.099
Finally, in the new prequels, we see the Illuminati
attempt to limit human augmentation, since

00:02:28.099 --> 00:02:32.460
having a bunch of engineered superhumans running
around isn’t really great for the whole

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.189
“compliant population” thing they’re
going for.

00:02:35.189 --> 00:02:39.590
If there is one thread that has run through
the sometimes vastly different games in the

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.500
series, it’s paranoia.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.520
Not only is there the conspiracy paranoia,
but also paranoia directed at so-called “outsiders”

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.520
and “others.”

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.520
“Damn, Clank!

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.400
Why don’t you watch where you’re going?“
Ultimately the games reveal the profound power

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.210
of paranoia and that it doesn’t matter whether
the paranoia points to truth or not.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:02.810
Paranoia, independent of truth, shapes our
actions, and ultimately, society.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.969
Early on in the original game, Gunther, your
cyborg coworker who yearns for a skull-gun,

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:10.879
is convinced that the facilities staff is
replacing orange soda in the vending machines

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.700
with lemon-lime in an inane and unlikely conspiracy
against him.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.940
"The machine would not make a mistake.”

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.129
“It's the maintenance man.

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:20.599
He knows I like orange.”

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:23.769
“So, you think the staff has some kind of
plot?"

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:24.769
"Yes.

00:03:24.769 --> 00:03:25.959
They do that on purpose."

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.049
Except, 20 years later in the game’s sequel,
it’s revealed in the ruins of Gunther’s

00:03:30.049 --> 00:03:32.219
office that he was right all along.

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:36.540
“Denying people their natural born rights
to choose their own artificially-flavored

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.540
destinies.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.079
Like I said, something’s wrong with that
machine…”

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:42.450
“Probably some sort of office politics.”

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:47.079
As if to foreshadow the entire rest of the
game, this idea of “just because you’re

00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:51.810
paranoid doesn’t mean they’re not after
you” becomes the main ethos of Deus Ex.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.769
In Mankind Divided, colleagues spin wild tales
of getting hacked, which turn out to be true

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.120
— “We have a lot of enemies.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.749
The people who bombed the train station, you
don't think they'd love to know where we are?

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:07.939
You need to help me figure out who's looking
into us and make them stop.“ Others suspect

00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:12.459
a police cover up of a bombing, "They're probably
destroying all the evidence there is right

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:13.459
now!"

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:14.459
Also true.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:15.709
"Well, I was right."

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:18.840
Even you, the player, must navigate who to
trust.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.900
Your old-time boss, David Sarif?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.150
Pilot Alex Vega?

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:26.530
Your new boss at Interpol, who may or may
not be working for the Illuminati?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.750
At every point, the game undermines your trust
in others: as you hack into the emails of

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.180
your coworkers, install listening devices,
and get ambushed by enemies who were tipped

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.570
off about your arrival.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:41.370
Hell, even the suicide cult that wants to
merge with computers in Mankind Divided turn

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:46.870
out to be only a few years off from being
right: JC Denton manages to do this with Helios

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.950
at the end of the original Deus Ex.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:53.990
So, why does Deus Ex make a point to validate
even the most far-fetched ideas?

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:59.449
It could be, in part, to tell a greater message
about how paranoia works in the real world.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:04.050
People who are paranoid often don’t invent
things out of nothing, but instead take interpretive

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.889
leaps when over-analyzing the data presented
to them.

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:10.140
"Well, if you thought he was high-strung before,
the attack only made him more manic.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:14.050
He’s making connections that no one sees,
and some that may or may not be there."

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:19.650
But rather than dismissing this kind of paranoia
as mere delusion, Deus Ex runs with it.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.370
Is a man rambling in the sewers about mind
control right?

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.370
"I was part of it, the - the - the hive mind.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.020
Inside the gate.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.790
I ... questioned.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:31.919
What holds us together?

00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:32.919
Where?

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:33.919
Why?"

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:34.919
Unequivocally, yes.

00:05:34.919 --> 00:05:37.319
"You mean your attempt to control people.

00:05:37.319 --> 00:05:40.770
Amplifying your hypnotic techniques with some
kind of social enhancer."

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:45.699
This brings me to one of Mankind Divided’s
most important commentaries: tracing the relationship

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:49.349
between general paranoia and racial paranoia.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:54.270
Augmented humans, as a metaphor for racial
discrimination, isn’t exactly subtle.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:59.069
As a mechanically augmented Interpol agent,
you face harassment from the citizens of Prague

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:03.199
— “F**king augs.” — and literally
live on the wrong side of the tracks as you

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:07.860
witness routine police brutality inflicted
on your augmented peers.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.770
To understand what fuels this discrimination,
we’re turning to cigar enthusiast and psychoanalyst

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:13.770
Jacques Lacan.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:16.760
Or at least, what the Slovenian Dumbledore
writes about him.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:22.870
And for Slavoj Zizek, our paranosid theories
often reflect on our own identities, ideologies,

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.879
and shortcomings, rather than the actual state
of things.

00:06:25.879 --> 00:06:30.650
For instance, he cites a story from Lacan
regarding a jealous husband, who, even if

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.880
right that his wife is sleeping around, is
still pathologically jealous.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:39.560
If she stays late at work, he’ll pathologically
assume she’s being unfaithful.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.200
If she starts having male friends, same thing.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:47.630
As a development of this logic, Zizek cites
Nazi anti-Semitism: if a Jewish person committed

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:53.330
a crime, it could very well be true, but the
fixation on Jewish crime spoke more to German

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:57.680
paranoia about foreigners and pure blood than
to any kind of real issue.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:03.130
In other words, crime is just crime until
a Jewish person commits it, then it becomes

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.300
part of the grand Jewish conspiracy to ruin
the German race, and so on.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:10.199
You can look at conspiracy theories in the
same light.

00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:14.099
Are most laws made in closed-door meetings
with lobbyist and interest groups?

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:15.099
Probably.

00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:19.139
Are they all part of a secret cult to serve
their reptilian overlords??

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:20.139
Probably not.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:25.509
Likewise, in Deus Ex, anti-augmentation advocates
filter all information through the lens that

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:30.210
augmented people are dangerous and possibly,
an affront to nature.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:34.670
Talking heads use terrorism or the catastrophic
“aug-incident,” where augmented people

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:40.139
were hacked into going into a homicidal rage,
to justify Apartheid-style oppression of augmented

00:07:40.139 --> 00:07:41.139
people.

00:07:41.139 --> 00:07:46.680
This discrimination then fuels even more violence,
thus making augmented paranoia a self-fulfilling

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:47.680
prophecy.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.890
"Everyone looking over their shoulder, terrified
augs like us are going to attack them again.”

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.070
“Somebody probably will.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.000
Treat people like animals long enough, and
they'll start acting like animals."

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.250
The power of paranoia to shape public discourse
can be seen in Deus Ex.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.330
Eliza Cassan’s defense of news coverage
meant to spread fear towards the augmented

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.751
is just “reporting the news.”

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:10.860
“But Ms. Akim, news outlets are simply reporting
on the current situation.”

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:15.189
And even if the reporting is true, her guest
points out: "You can choose to only show my

00:08:15.189 --> 00:08:19.419
shoe, which is very ugly, but that is only
a small part of me.

00:08:19.419 --> 00:08:21.790
News outlets only care about a small part.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.160
I'm sorry, Ms. Cassan, but you can't trust
the news outlets if you want to understand

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.160
the world."

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.310
The “aug debate” in the news functions
on two levels.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.310
1.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:36.029
As Akim points out, to only report on the
negative aspects of augmented existence, and

00:08:36.029 --> 00:08:37.029
2.

00:08:37.029 --> 00:08:41.539
To use augmented violence as a validation
for your larger ideological project: in this

00:08:41.539 --> 00:08:46.630
case, the Human Restoration Act - a bill that
would either remove or severely limit the

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.670
augmentations that people have.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:53.140
Of course, unlike real-world news, Picus’
news coverage is dictated by the Illuminati,

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.440
"Would they?

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:58.700
I was engineered to monitor communications
and data streams.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:03.579
To find out what people are talking about
and make sure it's being discussed correctly."

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:07.950
As they cover up evidence of water contamination
in Prague, and falsely report that a flight

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:14.750
was taken down by an augmented terrorist — "In
yet another augmented terror attack, 251 passengers

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:20.100
aboard Cista Airlines flight 451 were killed”
— rather than the truth that the plane was

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.220
shot down by a military installation.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.980
"Plane went down because of whatever the military
was doing there, not because of some augmented

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.160
passenger like Picus claims."

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:32.490
For Zizek, these paranoias don’t tell us
much about reality itself but instead shine

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.200
light on the reality behind the paranoia.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.279
For Deus Ex, that reality is a carefully constructed
story meant to combat augmentation, so that

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:44.690
the Illuminati can better control the population
for their pro-business purposes.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:48.899
But is there an even deeper truth to the way
paranoia operates in the game?

00:09:48.899 --> 00:09:53.200
While the real world, is not governed by the
Illuminati (depending on who you ask), one

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.810
could argue that it is governed by the basic
principle which the Illuminati in Deus Ex

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:00.820
understands: the state of exception.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:04.760
According to philosopher Giorgio Agamben,
there is a hidden law that lies behind both

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:10.360
modern liberal democracies and the totalitarian
regimes of the 20th century: the exception.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.880
We’ve talked about this before in our Walking
Dead and Attack on Titan videos, but Deus

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.350
Ex’s exploration is wholly unique.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:22.250
Agamben builds off the theory of sometimes
right but always-an-asshole Carl Schmitt,

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:28.140
who argued that what defines sovereignty is
not the law, per se, but the ability to suspend

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.550
the law - to make the exception.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:35.279
For Agamben, this suspension of law marks
all totalitarian regimes: the concentration

00:10:35.279 --> 00:10:40.510
camps were a physical space where normal law
was suspended for more than a decade: a state

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.010
of exception.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:46.269
Whereas our modern liberal democracies aren’t
building death camps, the state of exception

00:10:46.269 --> 00:10:49.490
is an always-imminent component of modern
governance.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:53.660
Usually in the name of an national emergency,
or an existential threat, governments today

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:58.459
regularly creates “zones of exception”
where the law no longer applies, or create

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.360
classes of people who are “outside” the
normal functioning of the law, and thus, exist

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.180
in this kind of exceptional state.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:10.610
Prisoners of war, protected by international
law, get replaced by enemy combatants, who

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:14.399
get sent to GitMo, where regular US law doesn’t
apply.

00:11:14.399 --> 00:11:18.860
In Deus Ex, this logic seems implicit to the
conspiracy-theory favorite FEMA.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:23.100
In the name of managing emergencies, they
build detention camps for political prisoners

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.959
and implement martial law.

00:11:24.959 --> 00:11:29.839
The segregated Utulek complex of Mankind Divided
presents a similar zone of exception.

00:11:29.839 --> 00:11:34.990
It resembles a mix of Apartheid-era South
Africa, Jewish ghettos, the Kowloon Walled

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:37.430
City and modern day refugee camps.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:41.820
The player witnesses horrifying examples of
police brutality and augmented people who

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.820
live in constant fear.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.649
All in the name of security.

00:11:45.649 --> 00:11:50.519
And when tensions boil over, such as when
an augmented rights activist is assassinated

00:11:50.519 --> 00:11:54.070
this civil unrest justifies even more repression.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:59.080
If the Illuminati wants to spread chaos, like
staging a train station bombing, it’s because

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:05.230
they understand that chaos breeds people desiring
security, and when people desire security,

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:10.350
it’s all the easier to suspend basic rights
and exert more authority.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:15.960
While we may think of chaos and order as opposites,
the game understands how they can become entangled

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:21.360
in the modern world: Chaos is manufactured
in discrete ways in order for oppressive powers

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.410
to maintain control.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:29.640
But besides illuminating - no pun intended
- how security operates even in our own non-Illuminati

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:36.329
world, Deus Ex also uses the state of exception
as just one of its many criticisms of transhumanism.

00:12:36.329 --> 00:12:40.660
Transhumanism is the idea that technology
will help us overcome human limitations like

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.600
disease and scarcity.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.190
Prosthetics, contact lenses, and in vitro
fertilization, are just stepping stones in

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.790
the greater transhumanist project.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.690
Transhumanism is baked into the very idea
of human augmentation in Deus Ex, however,

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:59.550
rather than blindly celebrating transhumanism,
it portends everything that could possibly

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:00.899
go wrong.

00:13:00.899 --> 00:13:06.149
As the human race unlocks human potential
and mastery over nature, that technology becomes

00:13:06.149 --> 00:13:11.700
available to individuals and groups, and can
potentially fall into the wrong hands.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:16.630
Even augmentation technology, developed by
the Illuminati, soon escaped their control

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.260
as private corporations entered the fray.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:23.949
This forced the Illuminati to change their
stance and oppose augmentation.

00:13:23.949 --> 00:13:24.949
“No.

00:13:24.949 --> 00:13:29.040
By going public with this discovery, Sarif
is forcing our hand.”

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:33.680
Invisible War starts with a terrorist attack
that turns everything into a gray goo, and

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.580
in Mankind Divided there exists an underground
market for augmentations, which is likely

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.560
assisting both the good guys and bad guys.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:47.459
As such, the destructive potential of technology
often necessitates permanent states of emergencies

00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:50.740
and martial law that Agamben’s work was
critical of.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:55.190
Basically as technology gets too epic, the
government will have little problem convincing

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:58.870
you that your rights have to be suspended
for the good of everyone.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:02.930
But it’s not just the state of exception
that’s a problem for the transhumanist future.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:08.850
JBS Haldane, one of the earliest thinkers
of transhumanism, warned in 1924 that society

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:12.740
would have a hard time keeping pace with the
progress of technology.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.820
In “Daedalus; or, Science and the Future,”
he wrote that “..the tendency of applied

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:22.001
science is to magnify injustices until they
become too intolerable to be borne, and the

00:14:22.001 --> 00:14:27.120
average man whom all the prophets and poets
could not move, turns at last and extinguishes

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.949
the evil at its source.”

00:14:28.949 --> 00:14:34.009
In other words, technology will make social
injustices worse, until societal anger will

00:14:34.009 --> 00:14:37.320
boil over into a full-on rage.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:42.570
In Deus Ex, more often than not, the dangers
of technology are thrust upon the poor.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:46.920
Those who are augmented need to constantly
take Neuropozyne to stop their body from rejecting

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:51.380
their augmentations, but those with means
can much more easily obtain the expensive

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:52.380
drug.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:56.779
And, in the case of manual laborers or soldiers
who are augmented by their employers, — “Let

00:14:56.779 --> 00:15:02.390
me guess, most of the laborers were augmented
with heavy duty industrial rigs.” — or

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:03.770
the government, — “Send you where they
want.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:04.770
Make you do what they want.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:08.120
Replace parts on you whenever and however
they want.”

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.940
— they exist in a precarious state where
the maintenance of their augmentations is

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:16.020
contingent on them maintaining the same or
similar job.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.820
Rather than suggesting that human evolution
through technology will level the playing

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:24.620
field, Deus Ex suggests societal forces will
make inequality worse.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:28.829
And just as Haldane warns that this tension
will cause people to rise up and root out

00:15:28.829 --> 00:15:33.800
evil at its source, we see two competing movements
in the game focused on this same thing.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:38.640
In Human Revolution, The Humanity Front uses
violences to stop the spread of augmentation,

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:43.250
and in Mankind Divided a legal solution exists
in the Human Restoration Act.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:48.089
Meanwhile, augmented people slowly entertain
violence as a political strategy, until the

00:15:48.089 --> 00:15:51.579
assassination of Talos Rucker results in full-on
riot.

00:15:51.579 --> 00:15:55.329
"You know word of Rucker's death is going
to spread, don't you?

00:15:55.329 --> 00:16:01.069
And when that happens, the head of state police
assures me Golem City will become a warzone.”

00:16:01.069 --> 00:16:05.570
Another idea trumpeted by some transhumanists
is the idea of the singularity a point at

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:10.180
which artificial intelligence will explode
the rate of technological development.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:14.430
In the original Deus Ex, Bob Page hopes to
create his own twisted version of this by

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:19.790
merging with the Helios AI, but instead, the
player is given the option to merge with Helios

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.920
to rule the post-singularity world as a benevolent
dictator.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.029
"You will be who you will be.

00:16:26.029 --> 00:16:27.810
We are our choices.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:31.810
We can choose to move humanity away from this."

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:35.920
The game doesn’t necessarily put any kind
of judgment on this, but the solution still

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.600
feels a bit icky.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:42.100
And afterwards, when the merger between JC
Denton and Helios doesn’t go as planned,

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:47.139
the technological infrastructure of the world
collapses, and chaos envelops the world.

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:48.139
"JC.

00:16:48.139 --> 00:16:49.139
The net's going...

00:16:49.139 --> 00:16:50.959
the net's going black!”

00:16:50.959 --> 00:16:56.519
The message is not-so-subtly found in the
name of the two AIs that usher in the singularity:

00:16:56.519 --> 00:16:58.130
Daedelus and Icarus.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.230
"We are Daedalus.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:02.339
We are Icarus.

00:17:02.339 --> 00:17:07.320
The barriers between us have fallen, and we
have become our own shadows.”

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:11.820
According to legend, Daedalus was an Ancient
Greek inventor who invented man-made flight.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:16.500
His son, Icarus, plummets to his death after
using his invention and flying too close to

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.500
the sun.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:22.410
The Collapse can be viewed in this light,
as a too-fast and too-reckless technological

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.640
development that comes, metaphorically, crashing
down.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.250
"You don't know what you're doing.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:29.990
Everything will be lost.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:30.990
Everything!

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.790
The world will fall to pieces!"

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:37.800
Haldane believed the only hope is for morality
to keep pace with science.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:42.080
Deus Ex explores the moral questions inherent
in our technology-driven future.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.770
Is it right for companies to augment their
workers?

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:50.860
Instead of asking this beforehand, the prevailing
logic in the game is: augment first, ask questions

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:51.860
later.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:57.100
What about installing chips to limit a person’s
augmentation if they say, go on a homicidal

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.100
rage?

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:02.331
A brief debate may happen on live TV, while
legislators are trying to pass the bill, but

00:18:02.331 --> 00:18:07.300
companies have already developed the technology
before anyone decides whether this technology

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:09.480
should even exist.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.690
Technology first, morality later.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.350
And that’s a recipe for disaster.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:17.720
In a way, Deus Ex is forcing us to ask these
questions.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:22.400
We can find Talos Rucker offering a robust
criticism of government’s limiting the abilities

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.780
of the augmented.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:28.530
And even though we’re a bit far from Jax-arms,
the games can make us question the technological

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.010
progress in our own world.

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:35.570
"Usually a humanitarian disaster like this
would get a lot of press and foreign aid,

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:38.030
but given that these are augmented people..."

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:42.900
Social media has radically redefined how we
engage with the world, and we’ve only begun

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:47.880
to ask questions about its influence, after
we suspect it has done something egregiously

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:48.880
wrong.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.010
So, what do you think Wisecrack?

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:54.800
Will art like Deus EX convince us to take
a critical look at technology before we decide

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.410
to universally adopt it?

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:59.760
Or are we diving head first into a nightmare?

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:00.960
And one more question.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:05.620
In a world where people trying to secede in
places like Texas, Catalonia, and even California

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:09.770
seems to be slowly getting more popular, the
original Deus Ex seems weirdly prophetic.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:14.450
There’s the National Secessionist Forces,
and Texas’ troubled attempt to leave The

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:15.450
Union.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:30.380
But how would that actually work?

